</script>

# Aspect Ratio

Displays content within a desired ratio. The box fills the width of its container and sets its height from `ratio` with the CSS `aspect-ratio` property.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { AspectRatio } from "#lib/components/ui/aspect-ratio/index.js";
</script>

<AspectRatio ratio={16 / 9} rounded="lg">
	<img src="/photo.jpg" alt="A city street at night" />
</AspectRatio>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/aspect-ratio.json
```

## Ratios

Set `ratio` to the width divided by the height, such as `16 / 9` or `4 / 3`. The default is `1`, a square. Images, videos, and iframes placed directly inside cover the box and crop to the ratio.

<Demo section="ratios" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<AspectRatio ratio={4 / 3}>
	<div>Any content</div>
</AspectRatio>
```

## Rounded

The box is square-cornered by default. Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to round it and clip the content to the corners. `pill` is a true pill and can clip tall content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for round corners that stay safe. The box has no padding or text of its own, so there is no `size` prop.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<AspectRatio ratio={1} rounded="lg">...</AspectRatio>
```

## API

The `AspectRatio` props extend the native `div` attributes.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Width divided by height, such as `16 / 9`; defaults to `1` */
	ratio?: number;
	/** Corner radius; square when omitted. Clips the content to the corners. `pill` is a true pill that can clip the content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` to stay round */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
